  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-019$qb$, $qb$A7-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$The record may be examined later during audit, governance review, or challenge to the original decision. Which note best records a decision made in a meeting?$qb$, $qb$Decision: use Vendor B; approved by Kavita on 8 July; Arjun to issue the order by noon tomorrow$qb$, $qb$Vendor B selected; Arjun to issue the order tomorrow$qb$, $qb$Team agreed to use Vendor B$qb$, $qb$Vendor discussion completed$qb$, $qb$Decision made$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-020$qb$, $qb$A7-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have two hours before a deadline and receive an optional invitation for a one-hour session. Reprioritizing one commitment will change several teams' plans and a senior stakeholder expectation. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Protect the deadline work and attend only if the session is more important or can be moved safely$qb$, $qb$Check the session purpose before deciding whether to attend$qb$, $qb$Attend because invitations should be accepted$qb$, $qb$Join the session while doing the deadline task$qb$, $qb$Ignore both the invitation and the deadline plan$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R2-021$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A standard report is delayed, but the person waiting only needs one confirmed figure from it. The workaround could become embedded across the operation, so efficiency, control, ownership, and auditability all matter. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Get the figure from an approved source, verify it, and provide it without waiting for the full report$qb$, $qb$Find the figure in another approved source and confirm it matches$qb$, $qb$Tell them to wait for the full report$qb$, $qb$Use last month's figure as an estimate$qb$, $qb$Guess the figure from recent trends$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
