  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R7-020$qb$, $qb$A7-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have three tasks due tomorrow, but one needs input from someone leaving early today. Changing one priority will force several teams to replan and may affect an external commitment. What should you do first?$qb$, $qb$Secure the needed input before the person leaves, then plan the remaining work$qb$, $qb$Contact the person now and explain what you need$qb$, $qb$Start the largest task first$qb$, $qb$Work in the order the tasks were assigned$qb$, $qb$Wait until tomorrow and ask someone else$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R7-021$qb$, $qb$A7-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A normal data source is unavailable, but two approved sources together contain the needed information. The workaround is spreading across teams and could become an uncontrolled operating standard. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Combine the approved information carefully and verify that it answers the need$qb$, $qb$Use both sources and cross-check any overlapping data$qb$, $qb$Wait for the normal source to return$qb$, $qb$Use only one source even if information is missing$qb$, $qb$Estimate the missing information$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
