  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-10TO17-R9-017$qb$, $qb$A7-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A deliverable due Friday needs two reviews, and each reviewer usually takes a day. The fixed outcome depends on external parties, scarce expertise, linked approvals, and minimal recovery margin. What is the best plan?$qb$, $qb$Work backward from Friday and schedule both reviews with enough time for changes$qb$, $qb$Send the first reviewer an early draft and reserve time for the second review$qb$, $qb$Finish the deliverable Thursday and request both reviews$qb$, $qb$Ask both reviewers to review it at the same time on Friday$qb$, $qb$Ignore review time when planning$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
