  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-1628$qb$, $qb$A7-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You have ninety minutes reserved to prepare evidence for an external audit. A teammate asks for comments today on slides for an internal session taking place next week. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Protect the customer response and agree a later review slot that still gives the colleague enough preparation time.$qb$, $qb$Review the slides now because it is quick.$qb$, $qb$Ignore the colleague until next week.$qb$, $qb$Review both at the same time.$qb$, $qb$Tell them to find another reviewer.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-1648$qb$, $qb$A7-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$While building a difficult recommendation, you keep refining slide transitions because that work feels easier than resolving a disputed assumption. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Stop cosmetic work, identify the evidence needed for the conclusion, and return to polish only after the reasoning is sound.$qb$, $qb$Finish animations first.$qb$, $qb$Alternate between animation and analysis.$qb$, $qb$Remove the conclusion.$qb$, $qb$Ask someone else to find the evidence.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-2361$qb$, $qb$A7-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$A supplier contract expires in four months. Re-tendering takes three months, while a product decision in six weeks may change demand. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Start no-regret preparation now, define the decision point after the product decision, and preserve enough time to avoid a forced renewal.$qb$, $qb$Implement a practical interim adjustment to address immediate operational needs while monitoring results.$qb$, $qb$Maintain existing procedures temporarily until formal company-wide guidance is published.$qb$, $qb$Escalate the issue to departmental leadership without first gathering supporting data or options.$qb$, $qb$Ignore the operational discrepancy and proceed with business as usual.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
